Subject: [PATCH 5/5] CP7 P19 staged suite: bounds-vs-single case; limit race
 locks the stage tables; plan note for the window cut

P19G_STAGED_BOUNDS_VS_SINGLE replaces the refusal-equality case: the staged
bounds are read back against the declared ones; at 100 targets x 1001 days
(100,100 cells) the single path refuses its unchanged grid cap while the
staged job completes with complete coverage and a reassembled analysis that
passes the frozen contract (semantic_hash recomputed server side); at 140
targets x 3660 days (512,400 cells, beyond job_history_cells) both paths
refuse with CP7_PLANNING_HISTORY_GRID_LIMIT and nothing is paged. The
statement-limit race locks every stage table but the job row, since units
read the stored reference and never the live tables.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
